sequenceDiagram
  %% Container runtime (docs/reference/development-containers.md#a-stopped-nested-fleet-clone-starts): `instance:wake` of a clone of a nested-fleet default starts the stopped copy and its inner fleet. A nested-fleet clone sleeps frozen and its wake resumes it (instance/wake.mmd); this start is for a copy that a host reboot, an OOM kill or a stop left stopped.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:wake
  %% kind: instance.start
  autonumber
  %% lane CL icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CL as Caller<br/>orbit · task flow
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>Instance container
  CL->>GW: instance:wake INSTANCE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:wake INSTANCE`
  %%> Callers:
  %%> - the command, after a host reboot, an OOM kill or a stop by hand left the copy stopped
  %%> - a Route visit to such a copy that slept: the runtime activation endpoint calls the same wake admission
  %%> - planned: the task flow before it uses a task's copy
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the caller is the Instance's Node or has node access to it
  Note over GW: Start or join the start<br/>one per Instance
  %%> When:
  %%> - an active development clone of a nested-fleet default, on a Node with the nested-fleet switch on, whose last sleep did not freeze it or whose wake since found it stopped
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the wake admits `instance.start` instead of `instance.wake`; an Idempotency-Key keys the start
  %%> - an open start of the Instance is joined; any other Operation on the Instance refuses it with `operation.target_busy`
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - a stopped nested-fleet default: `instance.sleep_unsupported`; it starts only through its deployment
  %%> - other lifecycle work: `instance.lifecycle_busy`; no run starts
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the run's one read of the Club key; without one the start fails before its run with `instance.nested_club_key_missing`
  GW-->>CL: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
  SW->>N: Start the container<br/>Ansible · tags start
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - a nested-fleet default's root disk grows to the intent's size first; it never shrinks
  %%> - the start guard: a nested-fleet container made before the keys first gets `boot.autostart=false` and `limits.memory.swap` equal to its memory (Incus gives no swap without a size), then the egress gates of every bridge NIC
  %%> - the presented machine name: a stopped container gets `/etc/hostname`, `/etc/machine-info` and the `127.0.1.1` line of `/etc/hosts` through the file API before the boot, so the boot gives the kernel and T3 the name; a running or frozen container gets nothing, and nothing restarts
  %%> - `incus start`, then the Club key into the container's /run (tmpfs) on stdin, the same script as the create's `clone-club-key`
  %%> - waits until each desired-running unit is active; T3 starts with the container, and the start does not wait for it
  %%> - a container frozen by a sleep resumes through the power helper's `restore`, under the Instance's lock: it reads the plan's pages back while still frozen, unfreezes once and closes swap on each cgroup of `limits.json`; a stopped container's plan is discarded before the boot; a start that left the container running removes the asleep marker
  %%> Why:
  %%> - no seed or snapshot holds the key, so every start delivers it before the fleet checks
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - `instance.power_helper_busy` when another power action on the Instance held the power helper's lock for 10 s, `instance.power_helper_failed` when the helper refused its input or crashed; either leaves the asleep marker and the container's power state as they were
  SW->>N: Start the inner fleet<br/>Ansible · fleet check, resume
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the create's `clone-fleet`: the fleet rules, the three nested containers, the tunnel `wg-nested` with the hub's resolver for `~nested-dev` and `~nested-prod`
  %%> - writes the copy's proxy bypass for units and login shells: the drop-ins and the manager environment
  %%> - restarts T3 once, only when the write changed something and this start booted the container (`last_used_at`)
  %%> - waits for Doctor over the tunnel and the three agents
  %%> - records its own seconds as `fleet_seconds`
  alt the run passes
    %% path: main
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
    Note over GW: Record running
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the runtime's `power_state` is `running`
    %%> - `nested_fleet_club_key` says what the start did with the key; `fleet_seconds` the fleet's time
  else a step fails
    %% path: failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - a fleet failure names why in the failure's detail, redacted
    %%> - the container may run with a fleet that is not ready; `power_state` stays as it was
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the same command; each step leaves what already runs as it is
  end
  loop until terminal
    CL->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CL: Status and result
  end
